./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1q4qhw/TASK-260715-1q4qhw_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:4071:EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-1y04r0_shared-tunnel-runtime/TASK-260715-3ejhyy_compose-m0-runtime-dependencies/README.md:4:Implement the production dependency factories consumed by ReluxTunnelCore using only the accepted M0 binding manifest from TASK-260720-1qhxqa. For each provider, construct candidate-neutral SSH bootstrap and transport, TCP and DNS consumers, an M1PacketPlaneSession wrapper over the accepted PacketBridge API, PacketFlow, NetworkSettingsPlanBuilder and NetworkSettingsApplier, clocks, metrics, logging, cancellation, memory pressure, and snapshot dependencies. M1PacketPlaneSession.prepare is pure preflight that validates bound configuration and constructs references without acquiring descriptors, HEV resources, the private SOCKS boundary, or PacketFlow reads. Its post-settings activateReads invokes the existing PacketBridge.start and owns the resulting HEV/private-ingress/bridge lifetime. Preserve deterministic harness substitution and prevent provider, HEV C, or selected-engine types from entering coordinator contracts.
